2. singular points of other gate shapes as functions of gamma (c = 1)
  Lorentzian in (gamma-1): 1/(1 + x(gamma-1)) has a pole at gamma0 = 1 - 1/x = 1 - 1.60222e-7  (inside [-1,1])
  Lorentzian in v^2 = 1 - 1/gamma^2: 1/(1 + v^2/v*^2) has poles at gamma = +-1/sqrt(1+v*^2) = +-0.999999919889 (inside [-1,1])
  Gaussian in v^2: exp(-(1 - 1/gamma^2)/(2 v*^2)) has an essential singularity at gamma = 0 (inside [-1,1])
  -> none of these has a Legendre (spin-tower) series that converges for gamma > 1; only gates entire in gamma, such as exp(-x(gamma-1)), can be built from a tower.
